do_1 = "sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift verifies kernel canonical receipts against an AuthorizedBatch today (sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift:42 MerkleProof; sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift:47 UInt32; sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift:179 ReceiptEffect; sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift:189 ProgramReceiptOutcome; sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift:216 ProtocolReceipt); add LocalVerifier.verifySequencerReceipt(receiptBytes, rawTransaction, keys) and the ReceiptKeys type implementing spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md:163-168 R2-R6: decode with byte-exact re-encode, receipt version 2 or 3, non-zero activity_id, ed25519 over sha256(\"LXP/v1/receipt\\0\" || unsigned preimage)."
do_2 = "In sdk/platform/swift/Sources/LayerXSDK/Verifier.swift check that context_hash equals a keyId of the pinned ReceiptKeys list (primary or standby) and that the batch_id height lies inside that key's [firstHeight, lastHeight] (spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md:165), that activity_id equals keccak256 of the raw transaction (spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md:166), and that seqHash = sha256(\"PAXEER/v1/sequence\\0\" || prevSeqHash || u64be(seq) || activity_id) (spec/layerx-merge/contracts/clients.md:168)."
