[task.12.33.8]
title = "Move the wallet and web exchange callers to the perps v2 open and cancel shapes"
status = "pending"
mode = "BUILD"
wave = 4
requires = ["9.33.13"]
reqs = ["9363.2"]
capabilities = []
interfaces = []
do_1 = "sdk/wallet/src/modules/exchange.ts: ExchangeModule.cancelOrder (:37) takes (orderId: string, accountId: string) and calls perpsCancelOrderCall(orderId, accountId) (:54); ExchangeOrder stays PerpsOpenPosition, whose v2 fields are marketId and accountId as 0x-prefixed 64-hex-digit words, side (1 long, 2 short), size and leverage (services/agent/sdk/typescript/src/perps.ts:718-724, from 9.33.13 per clients.md O58); openPosition pulls no collateral, the margin comes from the deposited cross account, so approval applies to deposit only."
do_2 = "apps/wallet/src/surfaces/ExchangeView.tsx:56-72: the open form takes marketId, side, size and leverage and builds { marketId: word(marketId), accountId, side: side === 'long' ? 1 : 2, size: parseUnits(size, 18), leverage: parseUnits(leverage, 18) } with pull 0n, where word() renders a decimal id as its 32-byte big-endian hex word and accountId is the connected address's layerx_account (sdk/wallet/src/types.ts:247, read as apps/wallet/src/account/KernelPlan.tsx:188 does); the cancel action builds surfaceModule.cancelOrder(word(id), accountId); the view refuses to build an order while layerx_account is null."
do_3 = "apps/web/src/app/exchange/exchange-client.tsx:168-175 and :235 build the same v2 order and perpsCancelOrderCall(word(orderId), accountId), with accountId the layerxAccount of pxResolveAccount(account) (apps/web/src/api/gateway.ts:253-261); the approve-before-open path goes (sendPerpsWrite is called with pull 0n for open and cancel), the deposit path keeps its approve."
do_4 = "apps/wallet/src/surfaces/ExchangeView.test.tsx:42-78 becomes exchange_view_opens_a_perps_position_through_the_v2_call_and_shows_the_decoded_event: it types marketId 3, side Short, size 50 and leverage 5, expects the preview to carry the selector of openPosition(bytes32,bytes32,uint8,uint256,uint256) and chain.sent to be exactly one send to the venue whose data equals perpsOpenPositionCall of that v2 order (no approve), and keeps the OrderPlaced event assertions; apps/web/e2e/exchange-perps.test.ts: the case at :195 becomes opening_a_position_sends_the_v2_perps_write_without_an_approve (one send, v2 data, no approve request), the cancel refusal at :241 passes (word(9n), accountId), and PERPS_ABI carries the v2 openPosition and cancelOrder entries."
do_5 = "Register every test named in tests as a case whose name is exactly that name (vitest it() in ExchangeView.test.tsx, node:test in exchange-perps.test.ts), because an anchored name pattern exits 0 when no case matches; the gate counts only when each run reports one passing case per name."
